From 321f251abdc22400cda57867c36b0258bd451fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fountain5405 <Fountain5405@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 03:34:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/27] ringct: check a block's sum checks over the compute
 pool

Why: verRctSemanticsSimple checks each signature's sum (outputs plus fee
against pseudo-outs) one by one on the calling thread, while the compute
pool waits. For a block of about 1,300 one-input FCMP++ transactions that
is part of a serial stretch on the block thread (with the BP+ batch and the
key-image checks) of about 5 of every 18 s on a 4-core Core 2 Quad.

The sum check moves unchanged into verRctSumsSimple. A batch of 16 or more
signatures is checked in contiguous chunks, one per pool thread; a smaller
batch, or a pool of one thread, on the calling thread as before. All sum
checks now run before any range proof is verified, instead of interleaved
with the gathering of the proofs.

Safety:
- The result is the same: true iff every signature's sum checks. An
  exception in a chunk fails that chunk.
- Only the order of two checks that both reject changes.
- Verification only; public data.

Tests: ringct.semantics_batch_accepts_valid, and
ringct.semantics_batch_rejects_one_bad_sum (a broken sum at the first,
middle and last of 64 signatures, the parallel path, and of 7, the serial
path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
